From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -write_style mux, a hold mux per bit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-write_style mux holds each word without a clock gate: every flop is
on the clock, its D the new data where the word is written and its own
value elsewhere, an AO22 per bit (the AOI22 and an inverter where the
library has none) and an inverter per word for the hold; a flop whose
output is inverted feeds back through an inverter per bit. The default,
clock_gate, is generate_ram's clock gate per word, as before. Which is
better depends on the design: a clock gate per word saves a mux per
bit, a mux keeps every flop on the plain clock. Not with -use_latch.

Tested: src/ram/test/write_mux_asap7.tcl.

Commit 8 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
